<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">

<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Results on <span id="S4.T2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">OfficeBench</span> and <span id="S4.T2.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">8-objective QA</span> benchmarks. We report performance metrics (acc/EM/F1) along with steps, peak input tokens (<math id="S4.T2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>), and dependency (<math id="S4.T2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{6}</annotation></semantics></math>). Best values are in <span id="S4.T2.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bold</span>. Rows in blue are <span id="S4.T2.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-bg-color:#E6F5FF;">ours</span>. <span id="S4.T2.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Acon</span> consistently improves accuracy/efficiency trade-offs.</figcaption><div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
