<figure id="A5.T10" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 10: </span>Results across different difficulty levels on <span id="A5.T10.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AppWorld</span> with <span id="A5.T10.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">distilled compressors</span>. We report accuracy (task goal completion score), average steps, peak input tokens (<math id="A5.T10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>), and dependency (<math id="A5.T10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>6</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{6}</annotation></semantics></math>). For all compressors, we use the optimized compression guideline after the utilization maximization <span id="A5.T10.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#D2691E;"> <math id="A5.T10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\underline{\textsc{ut}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#D2691E;" class="ltx_font_smallcaps" mathcolor="#D2691E">ut</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></munderover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\underline{\textsc{ut}}}</annotation></semantics></math></span> step. ‘Fine-tune’ means that we fine-tune small models with outputs from naive prompt before compression guideline optimization.</figcaption>
