<figure id="A5.F8" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.00615v1/05_distilled_abs_observation.svg" id="A5.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:548/136;" width="548" height="136"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 8: </span><span id="A5.F8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Results of distilled compressors on observation compression</span> with gpt-4.1 as the agent. Student models (Qwen3-14B, Qwen3-8B, Phi-4) are distilled from gpt-4.1 compressor using the optimized compression guideline after <span id="A5.F8.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#D2691E;"> <math id="A5.F8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\underline{\textsc{ut}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munderover accent="true" accentunder="true"><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#D2691E;" class="ltx_font_smallcaps" mathcolor="#D2691E">ut</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></munderover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\underline{\textsc{ut}}}</annotation></semantics></math></span> step, and evaluated across all benchmarks. We also include result with gpt-4.1-mini without distillation for comparison.</figcaption>
</figure>
